node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Playwright's local browser profile. It holds a real Supabase session, so it must never be
# committed. Screenshots from browser checks are build artefacts, not source.
.browser-profile/
*.png
# Scratch files from browser checks and commit messages. These are local tooling, not source, and a
# `git add -A` should never be able to sweep one into a commit.
tmp-*
tmp/
shot-*.png
# A crash log or a one-off scratch note lands in the root under some arbitrary name — `z.txt` was a
# Node stack trace that got committed, un-committed and committed again. The pattern above only catches
# names that start with `tmp-`, so it cannot catch a file called anything else. These are two shapes a
# `git add -A` should never be able to sweep in.
*.log
/z.txt
# Android wrapper build outputs — the android/ shell is source, its
# compiled artefacts are not.
android/.gradle/
android/.idea/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
*.apk
*.aab

